Description: Covers the steps of a mass spectrometry based label-free
    quantification (LFQ) analysis: quality control, normalization, aggregation
    of peptides to proteins, modelling, hypothesis testing and sample size
    estimation. A single function, build_contrast_analysis(), fits a model per
    protein and computes contrasts with one of many methods: linear, robust and
    rank-based regression, 'limma' and 'limma'-voom, 'DEqMS' variance
    moderation, the detection probability model of 'limpa', Firth logistic and
    binomial models of detection, mixed models and a median-peptide test
    derived from ROPECA on peptide-level data, a hurdle model combining
    intensity and detection, and variants that
    impute groups without observations at the limit of detection. All methods
    return their results through the same interface and columns, so they can be
    compared and combined. Models simple designs with one explanatory variable
    as well as experiments with several factors. Intended for proteomics core
    facilities and researchers analysing protein or peptide intensities
    quantified with MaxQuant, DIA-NN, Spectronaut, FragPipe or similar
    software. Developed while analysing dozens of proteomics datasets at the
    Functional Genomics Center Zurich.
